      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think I still prefer getting this off the `attributes()`. For instance, if the os2 table isn\u0027t present then this produces 9 (I think?), but using `attributes()` we\u0027ll end up with 5 since the default is normal. It\u0027s just a higher level interface and I\u0027d prefer not to essentially re-implement `Attributes.new` here.",
