      "writtenOn": "2024-03-18T12:01:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ll look into changing this back to `attributes()`, but the outcome if os2 is not present is different:\n`f.os()` returns a `Result` type, which is converted to an `Option` type by calling `ok()` on it. The `?` question mark operator checks the `Option` and if it\u0027s `Some()` unwraps it, otherwise `None` is returned from the closure, which results in `style` remaining unchanged and `false` returned from the function.",
